\subsubsection{How distant (in terms of iterations and/or time) the two methods are from the ground truth?}
For obvious reasons, the following investigation on the ability to correctly find the index of steady-state beginnings is only based on the set of steady time series as reference ground truth. 

Consequently, we analyzed both the raw differences from the ground truth and their absolute values to correctly assess a possible directional bias in model results, \kbkssd reliability, and accuracy. All the statistical tests were performed with a 0.05 level of significance.

