The neural network technique offers a large class of computational models in ML methods, inspired by the way biological neural network in the human brain processes information. It consists of interconnected layers of nodes, also known as perceptrons. Each of these nodes processes input data, collected from others through non-linear communication, defined by weights. Subsequently, it passes the result, added with approximate biases, to the next layer. The network is trained by adjusting the weights and biases to minimize the error between its output and the recommended result for a given input. Several regularization techniques are used in training the network to prevent overfitting and improve generalization. 
