\section{Pedal Prediction Robustness}
% \ziyunote{write something here: need a claim using italic.}

We observe that both baseline models, as well as our own, struggle to generalize from real recordings to synthetic data. To address this, we conduct a leave-one-out experiment showing that training on a more diverse set of room conditions improves our model’s ability to generalize to unseen acoustic environments. Further analysis supports our claim that \textit{current sustain pedal detection models are not robust to changes in room acoustics; moreover, their predictions are significantly influenced by reverberation, revealing a strong sensitivity to acoustic environments.}

