\section{Low-energy spectrum}
\label{app:spectrum}

While this work focuses on ground-state properties, examining the low-energy spectrum can give us insight into the formation of energy bands of different configurations (see, for example, Ref.~\cite{pohlmann_trion_2013}). In addition, it enables us to estimate the stability of the bound states. Thus, we show the low-energy spectrum for the examined balanced systems in Fig.~\ref{app:spectrum;fig:spectrum}. The panels show the spectrum of the full AABB [panel (a)] and AAABBB [panel (b)] systems, as well as their sub-systems.

