\subsection{Performance of the Pricing Algorithm on 10 CCBs} 
We observed the ``gap'' between the model price and market price by MREs (Mean Relative Errors),  MAREs (Mean Absolute Relative Errors) and RMSEs (Root Mean Square Errors),  these three indicators are used to quantify the differences in pricing.

They are defined as follows:
$$
\text{MRE} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \frac{V_{i}^{\text{mdl}} - V_{i}^{\text{mkt}}}{V_{i}^{\text{mkt}}}
, $$
$$
\text{MARE} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \frac{ |V_{i}^{\text{mdl}} - V_{i}^{\text{mkt}}|}{V_{i}^{\text{mkt}}}
, $$
$$
\text{RMSE} = \sqrt{\frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \left(\frac{V_{i}^{\text{mdl}} - V_{i}^{\text{mkt}}}{V_{i}^{\text{mkt}}}\right)^{2}}
, $$
where $V^\text{mdl}_i$ is the predicted  CCB price on the $i$th trading day and $V ^{\text{mkt}}_{i}$ is the corresponding market price.

