% Thermoelectric effects can be used to generate electricity from waste heat or to measure the temperature gradients.\cite{thermoele_1,thermoele_2,thermoele_3}
% Recently, the nonlinear term of Nernst effect, which generates a thermoelectric voltage from temperature fluctuation, was discovered in a bilayer of a type-II superconductor and a ferromagnetic insulator.\cite{arisawa_natcomm}
% This nonlinear effect, however, has been limited at an extremely low temperature $(<4\ \rm{K})$ to occur.
