(b) Under a negative electric field $-\bf E\parallel -\hat{\bf y}$ (a temperature gradient $-\nabla T\parallel -\hat{\bf y}$), the direction of the spin Hall (Nernst) current gets reversed to $-\bf j_{\rm s}$. The scattering intensity between the electrons in the HM and magnetization ${\bf M}$ in the FM, therefore, varies depending on the input direction.
