\abstract{Under the quaternion group, $Q_8$,  spin helicity emerges as a crucial element of the reality  of spin and is complementary to its polarization.  We show that the correlation in EPR coincidence experiments is conserved upon separation from a singlet state and  distributed between its polarization and coherence. Including helicity accounts for the violation of Bell's Inequalities without non-locality, and disproves Bell's Theorem by a counterexample.}

