   The first equality is the definition of $R$.

The second inequality follows from \Cref{p1g}.

The third equality follows from \Cref{dasdas} and \Cref{summe}.

The fourth inequality follows from \Cref{p1g} and the fact $w'(v)=w(v)$ for all $v \in V(T)$.

The fifth equality follows from the definition of $w'$ and the fact that $\kappa_{\vec{U}_1}(z_{in},v)=\kappa_{\vec{U}_1}(x_{in},v)$ and $\kappa_{\vec{U}_1}(v,z_{out})=\kappa_{\vec{U}_1}(v,x_{out})$ holds for every $v \in V(T)$ and every orientation $\vec{U}_1$ of $U$.

